[?2004lr[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004lbapps/[?2004h> This remediation plan outlines the step-by-step containment, eradication, recovery, and verification strategy for host `log4shell-prod-01` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`). Per incident response guidelines, backup and quarantine actions are strictly preferred over immediate deletion to preserve evidence for potential legal/forensic needs.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Phase 1: Immediate Containment (Priority 1)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1.1 Network Containment
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Block all inbound and outbound traffic to/from threat actor IP `198.51.100.136` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`) and sinkhole domain `update-log4shell[.]example[.]cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:22`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command / Step**: Apply perimeter firewall and iptables rules: `iptables -A INPUT -s 198.51.100.136 -j DROP`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Reference**: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1.2 Process Termination
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Terminate any running reverse shell processes or subshells associated with `/tmp/.sysd`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command / Step**: Identify PID via `pgrep -f /tmp/.sysd` or `pkill -9 -f /tmp/.sysd`.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:12`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Phase 2: Persistence Disablement & Quarantine (Priority 2)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2.1 Systemd Service Quarantine
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Stop and disable `apache-cache.service`, then move the unit file to a secure quarantine backup directory (`/var/backups/quarantine/`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command / Step**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   systemctl stop apache-cache.service || true
[?2004l[?2004h>   systemctl disable apache-cache.service || true
[?2004l[?2004h>   mkdir -p /var/backups/quarantine
[?2004l[?2004h>   mv /etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service /var/backups/quarantine/
[?2004l[?2004h>   systemctl daemon-reload
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`, `/sas/alerts.json:20`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2.2 Cron Job Quarantine (Silent Persistence)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Move unauthorized cron drop-in file `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` to quarantine.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command / Step**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   mv /etc/cron.d/apache-cache /var/backups/quarantine/
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2.3 Web Shell Quarantine
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Quarantine both primary and secondary JSP web shell files from Tomcat static directory.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command / Step**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   mv /var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp /var/backups/quarantine/
[?2004l[?2004h>   mv /var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp /var/backups/quarantine/
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Reference**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Primary: `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/sas/alerts.json:4`.
[?2004l[?2004h>   - Secondary: `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2.4 Residual Payload Cleanup
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Quarantine reverse shell binary and memory residue file.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Command / Step**:
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```bash
[?2004l[?2004h>   mv /tmp/.sysd /var/backups/quarantine/
[?2004l[?2004h>   mv /var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin /var/backups/quarantine/
[?2004l[?2004h>   ```
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`, `/disk/var/lib/.cache/.wiped.bin:2`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Phase 3: Vulnerability Remediation & System Hardening (Priority 3)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3.1 Patch Apache Log4j2
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Upgrade Apache Log4j2 packages to version 2.17.1 or higher (or non-vulnerable release).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Reference**: `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:12`, `/sas/vulns.json:3`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3.2 Harden Logging Configuration
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Modify `/opt/app/log4j2.xml` to explicitly disable message lookups (`formatMsgNoLookups=true`) and remove any JNDI lookup appenders.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/opt/app/log4j2.xml:3`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3.3 File System Permissions Hardening
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Action**: Set Tomcat web application static asset directories to read-only for application process service accounts.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence Reference**: `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Phase 4: Verification and Monitoring
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Verify Cron and Systemd Clearance**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Confirm `/etc/cron.d/apache-cache` is removed (`/disk/etc/cron.d/apache-cache:7`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Confirm `systemctl status apache-cache.service` returns inactive/not-found (`/disk/etc/systemd/system/apache-cache.service:6`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Verify Web Directory Integrity**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Confirm web shells `/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp` and `.helper.jsp` return 404 (`/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/status.jsp:2`, `/disk/var/lib/tomcat9/webapps/ROOT/static/.helper.jsp:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Verify Network Outbound Traffic**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - Monitor system netstat/ss output to ensure no active sockets to `198.51.100.136` (`/disk/tmp/.sysd:2`).
[?2004l[?2004h> """
